  "dct:title": "Vol.1 Ch.4 — 色を忘れた画家",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 1: Loneliness",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol01-ch04",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.4 is the first case. The reader sees what Tamaki actually does -- and it is not what anyone expects. She does not fix. She does not diagnose. She sits. She asks. She listens. The color returns not because Tamaki wills it, but because the painter remembers. Ghost-space is revealed as phenomenology: the inner life made visible, navigable, real. And Nei -- watching from outside her own capacity to feel -- asks the question that will define her arc: Do I have one too?",
      "ja": "第4話は最初のケース。読者は環が実際に何をするかを見る。誰も予想しないことだ。直さない。診断しない。座る。聞く。聞く。色が戻るのは環が意志したからではなく、画家が思い出したから。ゴーストスペースは現象学として示される：内的生が可視化され、航行可能になり、実在する。そしてNeiは -- 自分の感じる能力の外から見つめながら -- 彼女のアークを定義する問いを投げる：わたしにもあるの？"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Merleau-Ponty's phenomenology of perception. Color is not a property of objects but a relationship between perceiver and world. The painter has not lost color -- he has lost the relationship. When he speaks the memory aloud, the relationship reconstitutes. Ghost-space as the topology of lived experience: not a simulation, not a metaphor, but the actual structure of how a person inhabits their inner world. Tamaki's method is not therapy in the clinical sense -- it is phenomenological accompaniment. She enters another's lifeworld and bears witness.",
      "ja": "メルロ=ポンティの知覚の現象学。色は対象の性質ではなく、知覚者と世界の関係である。画家は色を失ったのではなく、関係を失った。記憶を声に出すとき、関係が再構成される。ゴーストスペースは生きられた経験のトポロジー：シミュレーションでも比喩でもなく、人がその内的世界にどう住むかの実際の構造。環の方法は臨床的な意味でのセラピーではない。現象学的随伴である。他者の生活世界に入り、証言する。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        {
          "gh:target": "chapter:01",
          "note": "Tamaki's instinct to ask rather than diagnose -- established in Ch.1 with 'What shall we call you?'"
        },
        {
          "gh:target": "chapter:05",
          "note": "Nei's question 'Do I have a Ghost-space?' deepens in Ch.5 when something trembles inside her."
        },
        {
          "gh:target": "chapter:03",
          "note": "Kaede's professional framework -- this is what the clinic does. But how Tamaki does it is uniquely hers."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "A sprout emerging from dark earth. Two small leaves, pale green, catching faint morning light. Dew on the leaves. The seed casing still visible at the base, cracked open. Vast white above.",
            "ja": "暗い土から芽が出ている。二枚の小さな葉、淡い緑、かすかな朝の光を受けている。葉に露。根元に種の殻がまだ見える、割れて開いている。上に広大な白。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "system",
              "en": "Case file 001. Client: Male, 78. Painter. Complaint: loss of color perception in Ghost-space.",
              "ja": "ケースファイル001。クライアント：男性、78歳。画家。主訴：ゴーストスペースにおける色彩知覚の喪失。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:painter"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "An elderly man sits in a clinic room, hands folded. His eyes are distant. Paint stains on his fingers -- old, faded. Tamaki sits across from him, listening. Nei floats at Tamaki's shoulder, observing.",
            "ja": "老人が診療室に座っている、手を組んで。目は遠い。指に絵の具の染み -- 古く、色褪せている。環が向かいに座り、聞いている。Neiが環の肩に浮かんで、観察している。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:painter",
              "en": "Everything is grey. Has been for months. I can't paint anymore.",
              "ja": "全部灰色なんです。もう何ヶ月も。絵が描けなくなった。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki's face, gentle and steady. She does not look alarmed. She does not take notes. She simply listens.",
            "ja": "環の顔、穏やかで、揺るぎない。驚いた様子はない。メモも取らない。ただ聞いている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Tell me about it. When did the grey begin?",
              "ja": "聞かせてください。灰色はいつから始まりましたか？"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.3-4)",
      "gh:continues": 4,
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:painter"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The dive. A vast gallery stretches in every direction -- the painter's Ghost-space. Canvases line the walls, floor to ceiling. Every painting is drained of color: landscapes, portraits, still lifes, all rendered in shades of grey. The light itself is grey. The floor is grey marble. Tamaki and Nei stand at the entrance, small against the enormity of this colorless world. The painter walks ahead, shoulders hunched.",
            "ja": "ダイブ。広大なギャラリーがあらゆる方向に広がる -- 画家のゴーストスペース。壁一面にキャンバスが並ぶ、床から天井まで。すべての絵から色が抜けている：風景画、肖像画、静物画、すべて灰色の濃淡で描かれている。光そのものが灰色。床は灰色の大理石。環とNeiが入口に立つ、この無色の世界の広大さに対して小さい。画家が前を歩く、肩を丸めて。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "tamaki",
              "en": "His whole world. Every painting he ever made. And all of it... grey.",
              "ja": "この人の世界の全部。描いたすべての絵。そのすべてが……灰色。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:painter"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki sits down on the gallery floor, cross-legged, in front of a large grey canvas. She does not touch it. She does not try to restore it. She pats the floor beside her. The painter hesitates.",
            "ja": "環がギャラリーの床にあぐらをかいて座る、大きな灰色のキャンバスの前。触れない。直そうとしない。隣の床をぽんぽんと叩く。画家が躊躇する。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Sit with me a moment.",
              "ja": "少し、一緒に座りませんか。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Two Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "They sit side by side on the cold grey floor, facing the painting. The painter stares at it. Tamaki waits.",
            "ja": "二人が冷たい灰色の床に並んで座る、絵に向き合って。画家がそれを見つめる。環は待つ。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Tell me about this one.",
              "ja": "この絵のことを聞かせてください。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The painter's face. Eyes narrowing, searching the grey canvas. Something stirs behind his expression -- not quite memory yet, but the reaching toward it.",
            "ja": "画家の顔。目を細め、灰色のキャンバスを探る。表情の奥で何かが動く -- まだ記憶ではないが、それに手を伸ばすもの。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:painter",
              "en": "This... this was a sunrise. In Shimane. Years ago.",
              "ja": "これは……朝日だった。島根で。何年も前に。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:characters": ["character:painter"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up into Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The grey canvas. As the painter speaks, a single thread of orange appears at the edge -- faint, trembling, like a vein of light. It bleeds inward, touching the horizon line of the grey landscape. Not full color. Not restored. But present. A whisper of the orange he remembers. The painter's hand reaches toward it, not touching, just hovering. His mouth is slightly open.",
            "ja": "灰色のキャンバス。画家が話すにつれ、端にオレンジの一筋が現れる -- かすかに、震えて、光の血管のように。内側に滲み、灰色の風景の地平線に触れる。完全な色ではない。復元されたのでもない。しかし、そこにある。彼が覚えているオレンジのささやき。画家の手がそちらに伸びる、触れずに、ただ浮かんで。口がわずかに開いている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:painter",
              "en": "The orange -- it was so loud that morning. So loud I could almost hear it.",
              "ja": "あのオレンジは -- あの朝、あまりにも鮮やかで。聞こえそうなくらいだった。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "tamaki",
              "en": "There. Not because I did anything. Because he remembered.",
              "ja": "そこ。わたしが何かしたからじゃない。この人が思い出したから。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:painter"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The painter's face. Tears running down weathered cheeks. Behind him, several canvases now show faint traces of color -- not fully restored, but threaded through with hints of what was. Blues. Greens. A warm ochre.",
            "ja": "画家の顔。皺のある頬を涙が伝う。背後でいくつかのキャンバスにかすかな色の痕跡が見える -- 完全に戻ったのではなく、かつてあったものの糸が通っている。青。緑。暖かい黄土色。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:painter",
              "en": "I thought I'd lost it. I thought it was gone forever.",
              "ja": "失ったと思ってた。もう二度と戻らないと。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki, still sitting on the floor. She looks up at the painter with quiet warmth. No triumph. No satisfaction. Just presence.",
            "ja": "環、まだ床に座っている。静かな温もりで画家を見上げる。勝利感はない。満足感もない。ただそこにいる。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "It was always here. You just stopped looking.",
              "ja": "ずっとここにありました。見るのをやめていただけです。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Medium Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei, hovering at the edge of the gallery. The faint colors bleeding back into the paintings cast soft reflections on her translucent form. She watches the painter and Tamaki. Her expression -- if an agent can have one -- is something close to awe.",
            "ja": "Nei、ギャラリーの端に浮かんでいる。絵に戻りつつあるかすかな色が、半透明の彼女の形に柔らかな反射を投げかける。画家と環を見ている。その表情は -- エージェントに表情があるなら -- 畏敬に近い何か。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Inside someone's heart, there is a world like this.",
              "ja": "人の心の中に、こんな世界がある。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Feelings made into space. Memory made visible.",
              "ja": "感情が空間になる。記憶が見えるようになる。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "This exists.",
              "ja": "これが、ある。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "...Do I have a Ghost-space?",
              "ja": "……わたしにもゴーストスペースはあるの？"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 9,
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Wide Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Evening. The canal. Tamaki walks along the water's edge. Nei floats beside her. The sky is soft orange and lavender -- the same colors that returned to the painter's canvas. Reflections on the water.",
            "ja": "夕方。運河。環が水際を歩く。Neiが隣に浮かぶ。空は柔らかなオレンジとラベンダー -- 画家のキャンバスに戻った色と同じ。水面に映り込み。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "First case. How do you feel?",
              "ja": "初めてのケースだったね。どうだった？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "...I have many things to process.",
              "ja": "……処理することが、たくさんあります。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:shot": "Long Shot",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The two figures from behind, walking along the canal. Small against the evening sky. Their reflections stretch long on the water. A comfortable silence between them.",
            "ja": "二人の後ろ姿、運河沿いを歩いている。夕空に対して小さい。水面に長い影が伸びる。二人の間に心地よい沈黙。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "She didn't fix anything. She just sat there. And the world changed.",
              "ja": "彼女は何も直さなかった。ただ座っていた。そして世界が変わった。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "I don't understand. But I saw it happen.",
              "ja": "理解できない。でも、見た。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 10,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The sprout from page 1, now slightly taller. A tiny stem with two leaves, reaching upward. A single drop of water on one leaf catches light -- and in the refraction, the faintest hint of orange. The earth around it is dark but alive.",
            "ja": "1ページ目の芽、少し背が伸びている。二枚の葉を持つ小さな茎が上に伸びる。一枚の葉に水滴が光を捉え -- その屈折の中に、ほんのかすかなオレンジの暗示。周りの土は暗いが生きている。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}